{
  "dom_id": "question-127237",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "Use the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ found in part 1 to estimate the value of $f(4.1).$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $f(4.1)≈$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Our tangent line approximation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =-7x+23.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(4.1)$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $x=4.1.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(4.1) & ≈L(4.1) \\\\  & =-7(4.1)+23 \\\\  & =-5.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
